    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Comancheria was the domain of the Nʉmʉnʉʉ, a people who moved from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshone">Shoshone</a> homelands onto the southern Plains around 1700.</li><li>Horses and bison sustained a decentralised society of bands and divisions that traded and raided from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>.</li><li>Epidemics, the destruction of the bison and US campaigns ended its independence; the last band surrendered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-sill">Fort Sill</a> in 1875.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1944 fourteen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> code talkers landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a> Beach with the US 4th Infantry Division, using their own language to pass army messages in Normandy.</p></aside>
    </section>

